  - Wilcoxon test
  - statistical validation

abstract: >
  This dataset contains all numerical results, statistical
  validation data, sensitivity analysis outputs, and
  publication figures supporting the paper under review.
  The repository includes best-found sizing results for
  four case studies and four algorithms (GWO, BBO, AO, ARO)
  under a rule-based energy management strategy,
  30-run statistical validation with Friedman and Wilcoxon
  tests, sensitivity analysis for the degradation parameter
  and sub-hourly peak factor, and real geographic tariff
  validation using SCE, Vattenfall, and ANEEL rates for
  three CHARGED city profiles. Key results: GWO achieves
  a mean TAC of $20,683/yr with CV=0.053% across 30
  independent runs (near-deterministic); SC integration
  reduces BESS equivalent full-cycle count by 21.1%
  (247 to 195 cycles/yr), extending effective BESS service
  life by 2.2 years; SC bank size is driven by local demand
  charge level, not by energy price or solar resource.
